.TH HYPRSNAP 1 "2026" "hyprsnap" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
hyprsnap \- screenshot, annotation, and live-drawing tool for Hyprland
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B hyprsnap
[\fIGLOBAL OPTIONS\fR] \fICOMMAND\fR [\fICOMMAND OPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B hyprsnap
is a GTK4-based screenshot, annotation, and live-drawing tool targeting
.BR Hyprland (1)
and other wlroots-based compositors. It captures pixels via the
\fIzwlr_screencopy_manager_v1\fR Wayland protocol, renders selectors and overlays through
\fIgtk4-layer-shell\fR, and draws annotations on a GTK4 canvas.
.SH GLOBAL OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-\-config " " \fIPATH\fR
Use \fIPATH\fR instead of \fI$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/hyprsnap/config.toml\fR.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Increase log verbosity (repeatable).
.SH COMMANDS
.SS screenshot
Capture pixels and pipe them to one or more sinks. With \fB\-\-edit\fR the captured image
is handed to the in-place annotation overlay before reaching the sinks.
.TP
.BR \-\-full
Stitch the bounding box covering every output into a single image.
.TP
.BR \-\-per\-output
Produce one file per output. Requires a filename template containing \fB{output}\fR.
Incompatible with \fB\-\-edit\fR.
.TP
.BR \-\-focused
Capture the currently focused window, queried over Hyprland's IPC.
.TP
.BR \-\-window " " \fIADDRESS\fR
Capture a specific Hyprland window by address.
.TP
.BR \-\-output " " \fINAME\fR
Capture a single output (\fIDP-1\fR, \fIeDP-1\fR, ...).
.TP
.BR \-\-region " " \fIX,Y,WxH\fR
Capture an explicit logical-pixel region.
.TP
.BR \-\-interactive
Open the selector overlay and let the user draw a region.
.TP
.BR \-\-edit
Open the in-place annotation overlay on the captured image before writing to sinks. The
overlay opens one layer-shell window per intersecting monitor so the captured pixels are
edited where they live on the desktop. Incompatible with \fB\-\-per\-output\fR.
.TP
.BR \-\-to " " \fISINK\fR
Add an output sink. May be passed multiple times. Recognised forms:
\fBfile\fR (write to the configured directory), \fBfile=\fIPATH\fR (write to \fIPATH\fR),
\fBclipboard\fR (write to the Wayland clipboard via \fIwl-clipboard-rs\fR; no
\fIwl-copy\fR binary is spawned),
\fBclipboard=\fIKIND\fR where \fIKIND\fR is \fBregular\fR, \fBprimary\fR, or \fBboth\fR
(per-sink override of \fB\-\-clipboard\-type\fR).
When running outside the daemon, the clipboard sink forks a short detached child
process that keeps serving the selection after \fBhyprsnap\fR exits so paste
keeps working until another client overtakes the selection.
.TP
.BR \-\-clipboard\-type " " \fIKIND\fR
Default clipboard selection (\fBregular\fR, \fBprimary\fR, or \fBboth\fR) used for every
\fB\-\-to clipboard\fR sink that does not carry an explicit \fI=KIND\fR suffix.
Falls back to \fB[clipboard].default_kind\fR in \fIconfig.toml\fR, then to \fBregular\fR.
.TP
.BR \-\-cursor
Include the hardware cursor in the capture.
.TP
.BR \-\-delay " " \fISECONDS\fR
Wait \fISECONDS\fR whole seconds before capturing. \fB0\fR is the same as omitting the
flag. The UI countdown only operates on integer seconds, so the CLI, config, and IPC
representations all match.
.TP
.BR \-\-via-daemon
Forward the request to a running \fBhyprsnap daemon\fR over its Unix socket instead of
executing locally.
.SS draw
Launch the live draw-on-screen overlay. Tool keys: \fBR\fR rectangle, \fBO\fR ellipse,
\fBA\fR arrow, \fBL\fR line (no arrowhead), \fBH\fR highlight, \fBF\fR freehand, \fBN\fR
numbered marker, \fBT\fR text, \fBX\fR redact. Other keys: \fBCtrl+Z\fR undo, \fBCtrl+L\fR
clear all layers, \fBCtrl+S\fR / \fBEnter\fR save via the zone selector, \fBP\fR toggle
pointer passthrough, \fBEsc\fR quit. \fBBlur\fR and \fBCrop\fR are editor-only and are
not available in the live overlay. \fBdraw\fR also accepts \fB\-\-via-daemon\fR to
toggle a daemon-managed overlay instead of spawning a new process, and
\fB\-\-toggle-passthrough\fR (requires \fB\-\-via-daemon\fR) to flip pointer passthrough
on the running overlay from a global keybind.
.SS daemon
Run the IPC server on \fI$XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/hyprsnap.sock\fR. Pass \fB\-\-systray\fR to
also register a StatusNotifierItem with Screenshot / Annotate / Draw / Quit menu items.
.SS doctor
Print a copy-pasteable Markdown diagnostic report covering version, runtime
environment, parsed configuration, and live capability probes (Hyprland IPC,
wlr-screencopy outputs, daemon socket \fBPing\fR). All headings are level 3 so the
output drops cleanly under a user-supplied level-2 heading. Always exits with status
\fB0\fR; failed probes surface as \fBWARN\fR / \fBFAIL\fR lines in the report.
.SH MODES
The \fBscreenshot\fR subcommand surfaces two interactive UI modes, neither of which is a
top-level subcommand.
.SS Selector
Shown by \fBscreenshot\fR without an explicit selection flag (or with
\fB\-\-interactive\fR). A floating toolbar offers Full / Screen / Window / Region modes,
a cursor toggle, a delay spinner, and a single action button:
.RS
.IP \(bu 2
\fBCapture\fR (\fBEnter\fR) commits the selection and writes the result to sinks. Holding
\fBShift\fR while clicking (or pressing \fBShift+Enter\fR / \fBShift+KP_Enter\fR) instead
captures and then opens the in-place annotation editor before writing. The button's icon
and tooltip swap live while Shift is held.
.RE
The Shift modifier ORs into the CLI \fB\-\-edit\fR flag: Shift-click on a plain
\fBscreenshot\fR opens the editor, and \fB\-\-edit\fR still opens the editor even on a
plain Capture click. Keyboard: \fB1\fR/\fB2\fR/\fB3\fR/\fB4\fR switch modes, \fBEsc\fR
cancels.
.SS Editor (in-place annotation overlay)
Opened by \fBscreenshot \-\-edit\fR or by a Shift-click / \fBShift+Enter\fR on the
selector's Capture button. Tool keys: \fBR\fR rectangle, \fBO\fR ellipse, \fBA\fR arrow,
\fBL\fR line, \fBH\fR highlight, \fBF\fR freehand, \fBN\fR numbered marker, \fBT\fR text,
\fBB\fR blur, \fBX\fR redact, \fBC\fR crop. Other keys: \fBCtrl+Z\fR undo, \fBCtrl+S\fR
/ \fBEnter\fR save, \fBEsc\fR quit. A color picker (with alpha) and a stroke-style
picker (Solid / Dashed / Dotted) sit next to the tool buttons; each tool remembers its
own color and style. The pickers are disabled for tools with hardcoded appearance
(\fBBlur\fR, \fBCrop\fR, \fBRedact\fR). The same pickers are available in the live
\fBdraw\fR overlay.
.SH CONFIGURATION
.B hyprsnap
reads \fI$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/hyprsnap/config.toml\fR. Every field is optional; see the
sample in the project README. Filename template tokens: \fB{ts}\fR, \fB{date}\fR,
\fB{time}\fR, \fB{output}\fR, \fB{selection}\fR.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/hyprsnap/config.toml
User configuration.
.TP
.I $XDG_PICTURES_DIR/Screenshots/
Default save directory.
.TP
.I $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/hyprsnap.sock
Daemon control socket.
.TP
.I $PREFIX/share/applications/noirbizar.re.HyprSnap.desktop
Standalone launcher (Screenshot/Draw actions).
.TP
.I $PREFIX/share/applications/noirbizar.re.HyprSnap.Daemon.desktop
Launcher for the daemon + systray (\fBhyprsnap daemon \-\-systray\fR).
.TP
.I $PREFIX/share/icons/hicolor/<size>/apps/noirbizar.re.HyprSnap.png
Application icon, resolved through the hicolor theme. Shipped sizes:
16, 32, 64, 128, 256, 512.
